135
00:06:59,130 --> 00:07:01,990
And then additionally,
there's also thromboxin A2

136
00:07:01,990 --> 00:07:03,970
that's released. This is,
again, helping with the

137
00:07:03,970 --> 00:07:06,630
vasoconstriction of
slowing the blood down so

138
00:07:06,630 --> 00:07:09,950
that all the platelets can
bind and form this clot.

139
00:07:11,130 --> 00:07:13,420
All right, so next
we have aggregation.

140
00:07:14,550 --> 00:07:19,630
so this is that newly
exposed receptor the gp2b3a

141
00:07:19,630 --> 00:07:24,390
it will now bind fibrinogen
so this helps even more

142
00:07:24,390 --> 00:07:26,890
for the platelets to aggregate
and it's a more secure

143
00:07:26,890 --> 00:07:29,570
connection between the
platelets platelets have

144
00:07:29,570 --> 00:07:32,250
multiple of these receptors
so you can can see in this

145
00:07:32,250 --> 00:07:34,530
photo that they're kind
of connecting to each

146
00:07:34,530 --> 00:07:38,330
other to help them create
this stable fibrin mesh so

147
00:07:38,330 --> 00:07:41,810
this is the last step in
the primary hemostasis and

148
00:07:41,810 --> 00:07:44,610
this is what helps form
that initial platelet plug.

149
00:07:45,610 --> 00:07:47,510
So we're going to pause really

150
00:07:47,510 --> 00:07:48,910
quick to answer a question.

151
00:07:49,370 --> 00:07:51,130
Which of the following has the

